# Line-ending policy.
#
# Added after a Python rewrite on Windows silently converted
# tools/repro/configure_linux.sh to CRLF, which made it fail on Linux with
#   configure_linux.sh: line 21: $'\r': command not found
# The reference platform is Linux (DEC-PLATFORM-001), so a CRLF shell script is
# a hard break, and it is exactly the kind of defect that only shows up on the
# platform the release depends on.
#
# Text files that are executed or parsed keep LF in the working tree on every
# platform. Checkpoint data, images and archives are marked binary so git never
# touches them -- several contain 0x0D bytes and must not be "normalised".

* -text

*.sh      text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.cmake   text eol=lf
*.H.in    text eol=lf
*.dat     text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
CMakeLists.txt text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore     text eol=lf

# PowerShell is Windows-side tooling; CRLF is correct there.
*.ps1     text eol=crlf

# Never normalise.
*.jpg     binary
*.png     binary
*.gz      binary
*.bundle  binary
exec/**/chk*/**   binary
exec/**/plt*/**   binary
contracts/USER_ADOPTED_DECISION_CONTRACT_20260801_V2.txt binary
